{
  "raw": {
    "http://fandm.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205675": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Student Accessibility Services",
      "description": "Franklin & Marshall College\nJob Posting: Assistant Director of Student Accessibility Services Franklin & Marshall College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Director of Student Accessibility Services Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Director of Student Accessibility Services Category: Student Affairs Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Accessibility Services Locations: Lancaster, PA Posted: Oct 9, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Exempt Position ID: 205675 Share About Franklin & Marshall College: Franklin & Marshall College, founded in 1787, is a residential college dedicated to excellence in undergraduate liberal arts education. The college thrives on forward-thinking growth, guided by a comprehensive new strategic plan currently under development. This vision animates dynamic new programs like the Venture and Impact Studio, which fosters student entrepreneurship, and the Mehlman Leadership and Performance Institute, which develops the next generation of leaders. Located in the city of Lancaster, the College integrates with the broader community, with the most recent example being a landmark eight-year partnership anchoring the college's baseball program at the professional Lancaster Stormers stadium. Exceptional Employee Benefits We support our staff with a competitive total rewards program designed to provide exceptional work-life harmony. Employees receive a generous 10% employer retirement contribution, alongside comprehensive medical, dental, and life insurance coverage plans. To support your family, the college provides valuable tuition benefits for eligible dependents, while also offering generous paid vacation allocations and recognized holiday closures to ensure ample time for rest and recovery. To learn more about Lancaster, please go to https://landinlancasterpa.com Job Description: Franklin & Marshall College is recruiting for a full-time Assistant Director of Student Accessibility Services Job Details: Location : F&M Campus - Lancaster, PA Classification : Full-time, Exempt Schedule : 40 hours, Monday - Friday. 11 months. Reports to : Director of Student Accessibility Services Department : Student Accessibility Services Approved Salary Range : Approved up to $58,000.00 annually Job Description: The Assistant Director of Student Accessibility Services (SAS) works with self-referred students to determine reasonable accommodations at F&M and maintains a student caseload. In addition, this position will be responsible for all technology for SAS. The Assistant Director of SAS reviews all requests for emotional support animals, keeps current records of ESAs, and serves as a liaison for off-campus property managers. This position plans and implements programming for the office, as well as provides disability-related presentations for the F&M College community. Essential Functions: Conduct intake interviews with students to assess needs and determine eligibility for services by reviewing documentation and evaluative reports. Maintain accurate, comprehensive, and timely student records, coordinate reasonable accommodations, services, and auxiliary aids, and prepare official letters of accommodation. Provide ongoing support through follow-up meetings and facilitate referrals to appropriate college and community resources as needed. Partner with F&M's Residential Life staff regarding student housing and dining accommodation requests. Work with Residential Life, along with off-campus property managers, on emotional support animal requests, record maintenance, and communication with students, staff, and other relevant parties about emotional support animals. Promote the access and independence of students with disabilities in the college environment by researching, recommending, implementing, and troubleshooting assistive and computer technologies. Provide outreach to the greater F&M community via planning and implementing programming related to disabilities. Assist with departmental efforts to provide education and training on disability inclusion and accessibility to the F&M community. Provide workshops and seminars on disability-related topics for the College community. All other duties as assigned. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree in Disability Services, Counseling, Educational Psychology, or related discipline. At least 3 years of relevant experience with disability and accommodation services. Excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills. Proficiency in Google Suite Products (Docs, Gmail, Sheets, Slides, Drive) Evidence of a commitment to community and belonging. Successful interview. Successful completion of background checks. Preferred Qualifications: Master's Degree in Disability Services, Counseling, Educational Psychology, or related discipline. 5 or more years of relevant experience with disability and accommodation services. Prior experience working in a Higher Education setting. Proficiency with the Accommodate software system. Additional Information: Offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of reference checks, a criminal background verification, and verification of credentials.  The College will coordinate these verifications. Full-time members of the Franklin & Marshall College professional staff receive competitive starting pay and a comprehensive benefits package that includes health coverage, dental, vision, generous retirement savings plan contributions, education benefits for employees, spouses and dependent children, and enjoy access to all College facilities including dining venues to suit all tastes, recreation and fitness facilities, and libraries, plus access to College performances, lectures, and events. To learn more about our Benefits, please visit our Benefits Page . Franklin & Marshall College is committed to having an inclusive campus community where all members are treated with dignity and respect. As an Equal Opportunity Employer, the College does not discriminate in its hiring or employment practices on the basis of gender/gender-identity, sex, race or ethnicity, color, national origin, religion, age, disability, veteran's status, genetic information, family or marital status, sexual orientation, or any other protected class. Application Instructions: All submitted materials must be submitted via this online process. We regret we are unable to accept applications or resumes submitted via mail, email, or fax. As you are submitting your application via this online process, please ensure that you provide an accurate email address. You will then receive an acknowledgment indicating that your application materials have been received. Individuals who need accommodations due to a disability in order to submit an application or attend an employment interview should contact Human Resources at (717) 358-3996. If you experience difficulty submitting your resume or cover letter, please CLICK HERE for assistance. If you have previously applied online to a position at Franklin & Marshall College and want to check on your submission or make changes, please CLICK HERE to log back into your account. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 415 Harrisburg Ave Lancaster, PA 17603"
    },
    "http://fandm.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=202547": {
      "title": "Dean of Admission",
      "description": "Franklin & Marshall College\nJob Posting: Dean of Admission Franklin & Marshall College \n\tJob Posting: Dean of Admission Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Dean of Admission Category: Enrollment Management Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Admission Locations: Lancaster, PA Posted: Jul 14, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Exempt Position ID: 202547 Share About Franklin & Marshall College: Franklin & Marshall College is a residential college dedicated to excellence in undergraduate liberal arts education. Its aims are to inspire in young people of high promise and diverse backgrounds a genuine and enduring love for learning, to teach them to read, write, and think critically, to instill in them the capacity for both independent and collaborative action, and to educate them to explore and understand the natural, social, and cultural worlds in which they live. In so doing, the College seeks to foster in its students' qualities of intellect, creativity, and character, that they may live fulfilling lives and contribute meaningfully to their occupations, their communities, and their world. To learn more about Lancaster, please go to https://landinlancasterpa.com Job Description: Franklin & Marshall College is recruiting for a full-time Dean of Admission. Job Details: Location : F&M Campus - Lancaster, PA Classification : Full-time, Exempt Schedule : 40 hours, Monday - Friday. Will require evenings and weekends. Reports to : Vice President of Enrollment Management Department : Admission Approved Salary Range: Approved salary range up to $140,000.00 annually. Job Description: Reporting to the Vice President of Enrollment Management, the Dean of Admission is responsible for leading the Office of Admission. This includes managing all aspects of domestic and international first-year and transfer admission recruitment, review, selection and yield in order to help achieve institutional goals. The Dean will work collaboratively with the VP to implement enrollment strategy and will liaise with internal and external constituencies. Essential Functions: Provide leadership for the Office of Admission, including domestic and international recruitment, visits, and events. Supervise the Director of Recruitment, Director of the Admission Visit Experience & Lombardo Welcome Center Manager, and Director of International Recruitment & Admission. Ensure successful operations of all areas of admission including, but not limited to professional development, staff compliance trainings and creating efficiencies. Collaborate closely with the Vice President for Enrollment and with division and office leadership. Develop, implement, and successfully execute on innovative, data driven strategies for recruitment, selection, and yield that are responsive to college goals for quality, quantity, net tuition revenue, and class composition. Develop creative, data informed strategies to build and maintain existing relationships with secondary schools and programs, school-based counselors, community-based, regional, and national organizations, two-year colleges, and campus partners to strategically expand the College's visibility and recruitment efforts. Ensure the effective implementation of these strategies. Guide the development and expansion of a visit program to build affinity and drive applications and enrollment. Collaborate with colleagues within and outside the division on the development of communication and marketing strategies that attract prospective students and families to F&M. Ensure that marketing and recruitment efforts are aligned. Partner effectively with the Athletics Department and coaches in the recruitment of student athletes. Advise in building a culture that prioritizes a sense of belonging for all students. Manage the admission budget. Provide a comprehensive admissions annual report. All other duties as assigned. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree. Minimum of 10 years in progressively responsible positions in selective college admission and/or related fields with a record of success. Demonstrated success at managing, leading, and motivating others at a college or university. Knowledge of a liberal arts environment. Knowledge of a recruitment-focused CRM. Excellent oral, written, interpersonal communication skills. Proficiency in Google Suite Products (Docs, Gmail, Sheets, Slides, Drive). Evidence of a commitment to community & belonging. Valid driver's license. This position works with minors (non F&M students under the age of 18) please review the link below that includes information regarding the protection of minors. Click HERE. Successful interview. Successful completion of background checks. Preferred Qualifications: Master's Degree. Prior  senior leadership experience in admission at a selective public or private Liberal Arts college or university. Knowledge of Technolutions Slate and other educational Enterprise System platform Additional Information: Offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of reference checks, a criminal background verification, and verification of credentials.  The College will coordinate these verifications. Full-time members of the Franklin & Marshall College professional staff receive competitive starting pay and a comprehensive benefits package that includes health coverage, dental, vision, generous retirement savings plan contributions, education benefits for employees, spouses and dependent children, and enjoy access to all College facilities including dining venues to suit all tastes, recreation and fitness facilities, and libraries, plus access to College performances, lectures, and events. To learn more about our Benefits, please visit our Benefits Page . Franklin & Marshall College is committed to having an inclusive campus community where all members are treated with dignity and respect. As an Equal Opportunity Employer, the College does not discriminate in its hiring or employment practices on the basis of gender/gender-identity, sex, race or ethnicity, color, national origin, religion, age, disability, veteran's status, genetic information, family or marital status, sexual orientation, or any other protected class. Application Instructions: All submitted materials must be submitted via this online process. We regret we are unable to accept applications or resumes submitted via mail, email, or fax. As you are submitting your application via this online process, please ensure that you provide an accurate email address. You will then receive an acknowledgment indicating that your application materials have been received. Individuals who need accommodations due to a disability in order to submit an application or attend an employment interview should contact Human Resources at (717) 358-3996. If you experience difficulty submitting your resume or cover letter, please CLICK HERE for assistance. If you have previously applied online to a position at Franklin & Marshall College and want to check on your submission or make changes, please CLICK HERE to log back into your account. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 415 Harrisburg Ave Lancaster, PA 17603"
