    "http://fandm.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205669": {
      "title": "HVAC/Refrigeration Technician",
      "description": "Franklin & Marshall College\nJob Posting: HVAC/Refrigeration Technician Franklin & Marshall College \n\tJob Posting: HVAC/Refrigeration Technician Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details HVAC/Refrigeration Technician Category: Finance & Administration Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Facilities Management Locations: Lancaster, PA Posted: Oct 9, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Non-Exempt Position ID: 205669 Share About Franklin & Marshall College: Franklin & Marshall College, founded in 1787, is a residential college dedicated to excellence in undergraduate liberal arts education. The college thrives on forward-thinking growth, guided by a comprehensive new strategic plan currently under development. This vision animates dynamic new programs like the Venture and Impact Studio, which fosters student entrepreneurship, and the Mehlman Leadership and Performance Institute, which develops the next generation of leaders. Located in the city of Lancaster, the College integrates with the broader community, with the most recent example being a landmark eight-year partnership anchoring the college's baseball program at the professional Lancaster Stormers stadium. Exceptional Employee Benefits We support our staff with a competitive total rewards program designed to provide exceptional work-life harmony. Employees receive a generous 10% employer retirement contribution, alongside comprehensive medical, dental, and life insurance coverage plans. To support your family, the college provides valuable tuition benefits for eligible dependents, while also offering generous paid vacation allocations and recognized holiday closures to ensure ample time for rest and recovery. To learn more about Lancaster, please go to https://landinlancasterpa.com Job Description: Franklin & Marshall College is recruiting for a full-time HVAC/Refrigeration Technician. Job Details: Location : F&M Campus - Lancaster, PA Classification : Full-time, Non-Exempt Schedule : 40 hours, Monday - Friday. Reports to : Acting AVP of Facilities Department : Facilities Management Approved Salary Range : Approved up to $52,000.00 Job Description: The HVAC Refrigeration Technician will install, repair, and perform preventive maintenance work on HVAC and refrigeration equipment on College properties.  The HVAC Refrigeration Technician will ensure that support is performed in a safe, effective, timely and professional manner while striving to provide excellent customer service to all members of the F&M Community. Essential Functions: Perform preventive maintenance on equipment in College buildings to include pumps, motors, air compressors, temperature controls, filters, belts, refrigeration components, piping and boilers. Install, maintain, repair and troubleshoot all types of refrigeration and HVAC equipment. Inspect HVAC systems on a daily basis and take corrective action when a problem is identified.  Coordinate and inspect any work performed by outside contractors. Daily monitoring of operating systems using various computerized energy management systems. Assist project managers in the design, installation and troubleshooting of new or existing HVAC and refrigeration systems. Perform on-call duties throughout the year.  Assist Special Work Assignment Team with College events.  Assist grounds crew with snow removal. All other duties as assigned. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Technical training or degree (Applied trades training). At least 3 years of experience installing, maintaining and/or repairing HVAC and refrigeration systems. Universal Refrigerant Certificate. Refrigerant Certification, minimum Level I and Level II. Excellent oral, written, interpersonal communication skills. Evidence of a commitment to community & belonging. Valid driver's license. Successful interview. Successful completion of background checks. Additional Information: Offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of reference checks, a criminal background verification, and verification of credentials.  The College will coordinate these verifications. Full-time members of the Franklin & Marshall College professional staff receive competitive starting pay and a comprehensive benefits package that includes health coverage, dental, vision, generous retirement savings plan contributions, education benefits for employees, spouses and dependent children, and enjoy access to all College facilities including dining venues to suit all tastes, recreation and fitness facilities, and libraries, plus access to College performances, lectures, and events. To learn more about our Benefits, please visit our Benefits Page . Franklin & Marshall College is committed to having an inclusive campus community where all members are treated with dignity and respect. As an Equal Opportunity Employer, the College does not discriminate in its hiring or employment practices on the basis of gender/gender-identity, sex, race or ethnicity, color, national origin, religion, age, disability, veteran's status, genetic information, family or marital status, sexual orientation, or any other protected class. Application Instructions: All submitted materials must be submitted via this online process. We regret we are unable to accept applications or resumes submitted via mail, email, or fax. As you are submitting your application via this online process, please ensure that you provide an accurate email address. You will then receive an acknowledgment indicating that your application materials have been received. Individuals who need accommodations due to a disability in order to submit an application or attend an employment interview should contact Human Resources at (717) 358-3996. If you experience difficulty submitting your resume or cover letter, please CLICK HERE for assistance. If you have previously applied online to a position at Franklin & Marshall College and want to check on your submission or make changes, please CLICK HERE to log back into your account. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 415 Harrisburg Ave Lancaster, PA 17603"
