    "http://fandm.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205101": {
      "title": "College Events and Protocol Director",
      "description": "Franklin & Marshall College\nJob Posting: College Events and Protocol Director Franklin & Marshall College \n\tJob Posting: College Events and Protocol Director Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details College Events and Protocol Director Category: Communications & Marketing Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Office of Communications & Marketing Locations: Lancaster, PA Posted: Sep 25, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Exempt Position ID: 205101 Share About Franklin & Marshall College: Franklin & Marshall College, founded in 1787, is a residential college dedicated to excellence in undergraduate liberal arts education. The college thrives on forward-thinking growth, guided by a comprehensive new strategic plan currently under development. This vision animates dynamic new programs like the Venture and Impact Studio, which fosters student entrepreneurship, and the Mehlman Leadership and Performance Institute, which develops the next generation of leaders. Located in the city of Lancaster, the College integrates with the broader community, with the most recent example being a landmark eight-year partnership anchoring the college's baseball program at the professional Lancaster Stormers stadium. Exceptional Employee Benefits We support our staff with a competitive total rewards program designed to provide exceptional work-life harmony. Employees receive a generous 10% employer retirement contribution, alongside comprehensive medical, dental, and life insurance coverage plans. To support your family, the college provides valuable tuition benefits for eligible dependents, while also offering generous paid vacation allocations and recognized holiday closures to ensure ample time for rest and recovery. To learn more about Lancaster, please go to https://landinlancasterpa.com Job Description: Franklin & Marshall College is recruiting for a full-time College Events & Protocol Director. Job Details: Location : F&M Campus - Lancaster, PA Classification : Full-time, Exempt Schedule : 40 hours, Monday - Friday. Will require evenings and weekends. Reports to : Vice President of Communications and Marketing. Department : Office of Communications and Marketing Approved Annual Salary Range : Approved up to $73,500.00 annually Job Description: The College Events and Protocol Director provides strategic vision, executive leadership, and comprehensive management and coordination for major college-wide ceremonies, high-profile institutional events, all presidential events, and strategic initiatives. Reporting to the Vice President for Communications and Marketing, this role ensures all events reflect the College's mission, brand standards, and level of excellence while providing a dignified experience for all attendees. The Director establishes and manages campus-wide event governance, protocols, and standard operating procedures. Exercising dotted-line functional authority over event planning personnel across all academic and administrative units, the Director oversees cross-departmental coordination, master calendar alignment, risk management, and brand execution across all campus events. The Director also personally coordinates events for the Office of the President, including events at Nevonia, the president's residence. Essential Functions: Ceremony and Institutional Event Management: Direct the strategic planning, coordination, and execution of College ceremonies and presidential events, including Commencement, Convocation, December graduation, Board of Trustees meetings, ancillary/advisory board meetings, various ceremonies and celebrations, and events at Nevonia, the president's house. Manage logistics and maintain a direct, hands-on presence for execution, run-of-shows, seating, staging, audiovisual production, catering, vendor contract negotiations, and post-event assessments. Presidential events and VIP Protocol Liaison: Serve as the chief liaison between Communications and Marketing, the Office of the President, Advancement, and hosting units for events involving executive leadership. Lead operational execution, protocol guidelines, run-of-shows, and host logistics for events involving the President, Trustees, distinguished donors, and external dignitaries, while collaborating with the Strategic Communications Director on event briefings, talking points, speeches, and messaging. Campus Event Governance and Dotted-Line Leadership: Serve as the functional leader and central authority and facilitator for event planners across all units of the College. Establish college-wide event standards, best-practice toolkits, and training; maintain oversight of the institutional master event calendar to eliminate scheduling conflicts, promote sustainable, eco-friendly event practices when possible, and align college brand messaging. Budget and Vendor Management: Develop and manage operating budgets associated with signature ceremonies and institutional events, monitoring expenditures and negotiating high-value contracts with key campus vendors (e.g., printing, catering, security, florists, rental companies). Event Operations, Safety, and Compliance: Serve as the primary operational partner to Dining Services, Facilities, ITS/AV, Public Safety, and Accessibility Services to establish emergency action plans, weather contingency plans, and ADA compliance standards for major public gatherings. Team Recruitment and Leadership: Recruit, train, mentor, and manage event support teams, including student workers, staff partners, and volunteers, fostering professional development and high service standards. Institutional Representation: Represent the priorities of the Communications and Marketing division and executive leadership by serving on designated College committees. All other duties as assigned. Requirements: Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree, with preferred specialties' in event management, hospitality, communications, public relations, business administration, or a related field. At least 5 years of progressive project management, executive event planning, and institutional protocol experience. Demonstrated experience directing large-scale ceremonial, high-profile, and executive events. Demonstrated capability to exercise matrixed leadership, establish timelines, and build effective relationships with campus stakeholders. Excellent oral, written, interpersonal communication skills. Proficiency in Google Suite Products (Docs, Gmail, Sheets, Slides, Drive) Evidence of a commitment to community & belonging. Valid driver's license. Successful interview. Successful completion of background checks. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in communications, marketing, higher education administration, or related discipline. Prior professional work experience supporting executive leadership or central communications within a higher education environment, ideally at a small liberal arts college. 7 or more years of experience in high-level event management and institutional governance. Additional Information: Offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of reference checks, a criminal background verification, and verification of credentials.  The College will coordinate these verifications. Full-time members of the Franklin & Marshall College professional staff receive competitive starting pay and a comprehensive benefits package that includes health coverage, dental, vision, generous retirement savings plan contributions, education benefits for employees, spouses and dependent children, and enjoy access to all College facilities including dining venues to suit all tastes, recreation and fitness facilities, and libraries, plus access to College performances, lectures, and events. To learn more about our Benefits, please visit our Benefits Page . Franklin & Marshall College is committed to having an inclusive campus community where all members are treated with dignity and respect. As an Equal Opportunity Employer, the College does not discriminate in its hiring or employment practices on the basis of gender/gender-identity, sex, race or ethnicity, color, national origin, religion, age, disability, veteran's status, genetic information, family or marital status, sexual orientation, or any other protected class. Application Instructions: All submitted materials must be submitted via this online process. We regret we are unable to accept applications or resumes submitted via mail, email, or fax. As you are submitting your application via this online process, please ensure that you provide an accurate email address. You will then receive an acknowledgment indicating that your application materials have been received. Individuals who need accommodations due to a disability in order to submit an application or attend an employment interview should contact Human Resources at (717) 358-3996. If you experience difficulty submitting your resume or cover letter, please CLICK HERE for assistance. If you have previously applied online to a position at Franklin & Marshall College and want to check on your submission or make changes, please CLICK HERE to log back into your account. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 415 Harrisburg Ave Lancaster, PA 17603"
    },
    "http://fandm.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204811": {
      "title": "Assistant Secretary to the Board & Executive Project Manager",
      "description": "Franklin & Marshall College\nJob Posting: Assistant Secretary to the Board & Executive Project Manager Franklin & Marshall College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Secretary to the Board & Executive Project Manager Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Secretary to the Board & Executive Project Manager Category: Office of the President Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Office of the President Locations: Lancaster, PA Posted: Sep 15, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Exempt Position ID: 204811 Share About Franklin & Marshall College: Franklin & Marshall College is a residential college dedicated to excellence in undergraduate liberal arts education. Its aims are to inspire in young people of high promise and diverse backgrounds a genuine and enduring love for learning, to teach them to read, write, and think critically, to instill in them the capacity for both independent and collaborative action, and to educate them to explore and understand the natural, social, and cultural worlds in which they live. In so doing, the College seeks to foster in its students' qualities of intellect, creativity, and character, that they may live fulfilling lives and contribute meaningfully to their occupations, their communities, and their world. To learn more about Lancaster, please go to https://landinlancasterpa.com Job Description: Franklin & Marshall College is recruiting for a full-time Assistant Secretary to the Board & Executive Project Manager. Job Details: Location : F&M Campus - Lancaster, PA Classification : Full-time, Exempt Schedule : 40 hours, Monday - Friday. Will require evenings and weekends. Reports to : Vice President, General Counsel & Secretary to the Board Department : Office of the President Approved Salary Range : $67,500.00 - $72,500.00 Job Description: The Assistant Board Secretary and Executive Project Manager provides administrative, operational, project support and management to the President, Chief of Staff and Secretary to the Board of Franklin & Marshall College. This dual-focused role ensures seamless governance operations while supporting institutional programs and strategic initiatives coming out of the Office of the President. Serving to ensure smooth operations, communications, and execution around the board and other special projects, this position manages projects and facilitates work among trustees, the President, and college leadership. The ideal candidate possesses a high degree of discretion, exceptional organizational capabilities, excellent communication skills, and strong abilities to manage and execute projects. Essential Functions: Coordinate end-to-end logistics for Board and committee meetings, including scheduling, venue arrangements, catering, technology setup, managing invitations and RSVPs, and assembling event materials. Lead, track, and complete special administrative projects and strategic initiatives assigned by the President, Chief of Staff, or Secretary to the Board. Draft and distribute meeting agendas under the direction of the Secretary to the Board. Attend Board meetings to record accurate minutes and provide real-time administrative support, maintaining accurate, organized, and secure electronic and physical files for Board records. Research, compile, and prepare comprehensive briefs, reports, and presentation materials for executive review and institutional decision-making. Maintain updated trustee contact lists and committee records while facilitating clear, continuous communication between trustees and the Office of the President through mailings, announcements, and emails. Collaborate with college leadership and departmental stakeholders to track progress on institutional priorities originating from the Office of the President. Maintain high familiarity with College Bylaws and governing documents to guide administrative processes. Research and compile information on governance best practices to support ongoing Board development initiatives. Perform all other duties as assigned by the President, Chief of Staff or the Secretary to the Board. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree or equivalent combination of experience and training. At least 5 years of relevant experience with administrative and clerical procedures. Prior experience supporting executive leadership, governance boards, or managing cross-departmental projects. High level of accuracy in minute-taking, records management, and document preparation. A high degree of professionalism and the ability to maintain strict confidentiality. Excellent oral, written, interpersonal communication skills. Proficiency in Google Suite Products (Docs, Gmail, Sheets, Slides, Drive) Technical proficiency in relevant applications such as MS Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint). Attention to detail. Evidence of a commitment to community and belonging. Successful interview. Successful completion of background checks. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working in higher education or non-profit sectors. Prior work experience in an executive office environment. Additional Information: Offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of reference checks, a criminal background verification, and verification of credentials.  The College will coordinate these verifications. Full-time members of the Franklin & Marshall College professional staff receive competitive starting pay and a comprehensive benefits package that includes health coverage, dental, vision, generous retirement savings plan contributions, education benefits for employees, spouses and dependent children, and enjoy access to all College facilities including dining venues to suit all tastes, recreation and fitness facilities, and libraries, plus access to College performances, lectures, and events. To learn more about our Benefits, please visit our Benefits Page . Franklin & Marshall College is committed to having an inclusive campus community where all members are treated with dignity and respect. As an Equal Opportunity Employer, the College does not discriminate in its hiring or employment practices on the basis of gender/gender-identity, sex, race or ethnicity, color, national origin, religion, age, disability, veteran's status, genetic information, family or marital status, sexual orientation, or any other protected class. Application Instructions: All submitted materials must be submitted via this online process. We regret we are unable to accept applications or resumes submitted via mail, email, or fax. As you are submitting your application via this online process, please ensure that you provide an accurate email address. You will then receive an acknowledgment indicating that your application materials have been received. Individuals who need accommodations due to a disability in order to submit an application or attend an employment interview should contact Human Resources at (717) 358-3996. If you experience difficulty submitting your resume or cover letter, please CLICK HERE for assistance. If you have previously applied online to a position at Franklin & Marshall College and want to check on your submission or make changes, please CLICK HERE to log back into your account. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 415 Harrisburg Ave Lancaster, PA 17603"
